  "description": "Boundary cases of the OpenAPI source-document bounds that Server scan preparation (internal/scanplan) and the Runtime OpenAPI authoring Toolset openapi@1 both enforce: LIM-SCN-39 UTF-8 source bytes; LIM-SCN-41 depth, with the top-level value at depth 1 and every member name, member value and array element one deeper than its container; and LIM-SCN-42 nodes, counting every object, array, scalar and member name. Each case is generated at test time in both formats, so no large payload is checked in. A document is the format's prefix followed, in this order and only when the case sets them, by x-deep (deep.depth - 2 nested one-member objects {\"a\": ...} or arrays around the number 0, so the 0 is at deep.depth), x-items (an array of elements zeros), x-keys (an object of members members k000000, k000001, ..., each 0) and x-pad (a string of pad.fill repeated, then completed with a, so the document has exactly pad.bytes bytes). JSON is compact; YAML uses block mappings and sequences with two-space indentation and a flow sequence for nested arrays. sha256 pins each generated document so both readers test identical bytes; nodes and depth describe the document; violation names the one bound a rejected document exceeds and is null for an accepted one.",
